### Manual smoke test — VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client.
### Run top to bottom; later requests reuse variables captured from earlier ones.

@host = http://localhost:4000
@email = demo@example.com
@password = CorrectHorse1

### Liveness
GET {{host}}/health

### Readiness (verifies the database connection)
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### Register — 201, sets the refresh cookie
# @name register
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "name": "Demo User"
}

@accessToken = {{register.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### Duplicate email — expect 409 CONFLICT
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Weak password — expect 422 with per-field details
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "weak@example.com", "password": "weak" }

### Role injection is ignored — response shows "role": "USER"
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "escalate@example.com", "password": "{{password}}", "role": "ADMIN" }

### Login — 200, new session
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

@loginToken = {{login.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### Wrong password — expect 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "WrongPassword1" }

### Unknown email — byte-identical response to the request above
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nobody@example.com", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Protected route — 200. Verified in memory, no database query.
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{loginToken}}

### No token — expect 401
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me

### Garbage token — expect 401 TOKEN_INVALID
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer not.a.real.jwt

### Swagger UI (open in a browser)
GET {{host}}/api/docs

### Raw OpenAPI spec — import into Postman / feed to a client generator
GET {{host}}/api/docs.json

### Refresh — uses the cookie the client already holds. No Authorization header.
### Returns a new access token AND rotates the refresh cookie.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh

### Refresh again — works, because the client now holds the rotated cookie.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh

### Logout — deletes the refresh token row and clears the cookie
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout

### Refresh after logout — expect 401. This is what server-side storage buys.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh

### Sign out everywhere (needs a fresh login first)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout-all
Authorization: Bearer {{loginToken}}

### Unknown route — expect 404 in the standard envelope
GET {{host}}/api/nope


### ==========================================================================
### RBAC
### ==========================================================================

### Sign in as Super Admin (holds "*")
# @name su
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "superadmin@example.com", "password": "SuperAdmin123!" }

@su = {{su.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### Sign in as a plain user (read-only)
# @name plain
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "user@example.com", "password": "User1234!" }

@plain = {{plain.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### Super Admin can list roles — expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{su}}

### Plain user cannot — expect 403, message names "role.view"
GET {{host}}/api/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{plain}}

### No token at all — expect 401 (not 403)
GET {{host}}/api/roles

### List permissions, grouped by module
GET {{host}}/api/permissions?limit=100
Authorization: Bearer {{su}}

### Filter permissions to one module
GET {{host}}/api/permissions?resource=employee
Authorization: Bearer {{su}}

### --- Adding a brand new module, with no code change ---

### 1. Register the capability — resource/operation are derived
# @name newPerm
POST {{host}}/api/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{su}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "invoice.approve", "description": "Approve invoices" }

### 2. Create a role that grants it
# @name approver
POST {{host}}/api/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{su}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "invoice_approver",
  "displayName": "Invoice Approver",
  "permissions": ["invoice.approve"]
}

@roleId = {{approver.response.body.data.role.id}}

### 3. Gate a route with authorize("invoice.approve") — Super Admin already passes it.

### Unknown permission is rejected and named — expect 422
POST {{host}}/api/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{su}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "broken_role", "displayName": "Broken", "permissions": ["typo.oops"] }

### Replace a role's grants (transactional)
PUT {{host}}/api/roles/{{roleId}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{su}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "permissions": ["invoice.approve", "employee.view"] }

### Add grants incrementally
POST {{host}}/api/roles/{{roleId}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{su}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "permissions": ["department.view"] }

### Revoke grants
DELETE {{host}}/api/roles/{{roleId}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{su}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "permissions": ["department.view"] }

### --- Assigning roles to users ---

### Find a user
# @name users
GET {{host}}/api/users?search=manager@example.com
Authorization: Bearer {{su}}

@userId = {{users.response.body.data.users.0.id}}

### Give them TWO roles at once — permissions become the union.
### This also deletes that user's refresh tokens, so the change applies immediately.
PUT {{host}}/api/users/{{userId}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{su}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roles": ["manager", "invoice_approver"] }

### Add a role without removing existing ones
POST {{host}}/api/users/{{userId}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{su}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roles": ["user"] }

### Remove a role
DELETE {{host}}/api/users/{{userId}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{su}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roles": ["invoice_approver"] }

### --- Guard rails (all expected to fail) ---

### Plain user cannot promote themselves — expect 403
PUT {{host}}/api/users/{{userId}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{plain}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roles": ["super_admin"] }

### Cleanup: delete the demo role (works only once nobody holds it)
DELETE {{host}}/api/roles/{{roleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{su}}

### ==========================================================================
### Lead engine
### ==========================================================================
###
### Walks one lead through the whole journey, then reads the funnel.
### Sign in as the acme admin first — it holds lead.*, lead_source.* and
### lead_stage.*.

### Log in as the acme admin
# @name leadAdmin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@example.com", "password": "Admin123!" }

@la = {{leadAdmin.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### The pipeline, provisioned on first use
GET {{host}}/api/lead-stages
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}

### Sources — one per channel out of the box
GET {{host}}/api/lead-sources
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}

### --- Capture from every channel ---

### WhatsApp enquiry
# @name captured
POST {{host}}/api/leads/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel": "WHATSAPP",
  "firstName": "Ravi",
  "lastName": "Menon",
  "phone": "+91 90000 11111",
  "company": "Vertex Logistics",
  "externalId": "wa-88213",
  "campaign": "diwali-2026",
  "utmSource": "whatsapp",
  "utmMedium": "social",
  "landingPage": "https://acme.example.com/quote",
  "estimatedValue": 125000
}

@leadId = {{captured.response.body.data.lead.id}}

### Website form
POST {{host}}/api/leads/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel": "WEBSITE_FORM",
  "email": "priya@nimbus.example.com",
  "company": "Nimbus Interiors",
  "utmSource": "google",
  "utmMedium": "cpc",
  "utmCampaign": "diwali-2026"
}

### Google Ads lead form
POST {{host}}/api/leads/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "channel": "GOOGLE_ADS", "email": "buyer@kestrel.example.com", "company": "Kestrel Foods" }

### Redelivered webhook — expect 200, outcome "duplicate_external_id", no new lead
POST {{host}}/api/leads/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "channel": "WHATSAPP", "phone": "+91 90000 11111", "externalId": "wa-88213" }

### Repeat enquiry from another channel — expect 200, "merged_into_open_lead"
POST {{host}}/api/leads/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "channel": "INSTAGRAM", "phone": "+91 90000 11111", "jobTitle": "Ops Head" }

### Capture cannot set a stage, owner or status — they are stripped, not rejected
POST {{host}}/api/leads/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "channel": "EMAIL", "email": "sneaky@example.com", "stageKey": "won", "status": "WON" }

### A lead nobody can be reached at — expect 422
POST {{host}}/api/leads/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "channel": "EMAIL", "firstName": "Anon", "company": "No Contact Ltd" }

### --- Work the lead ---

### Who can own it
GET {{host}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}

### Assign it (paste a userId from above)
PUT {{host}}/api/leads/{{leadId}}/assignment
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "assignedToId": "REPLACE_WITH_USER_ID", "note": "Ravi covers logistics" }

### Log an outbound call — this is what turns "received" into "contacted"
POST {{host}}/api/leads/{{leadId}}/activities
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "CALL", "direction": "OUTBOUND", "subject": "Intro call", "durationMinutes": 12 }

### Their reply — "contacted" becomes "replied". Direction is the whole difference.
POST {{host}}/api/leads/{{leadId}}/activities
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "WHATSAPP", "direction": "INBOUND", "body": "Send me a quote for 400 units" }

### Meeting booked
POST {{host}}/api/leads/{{leadId}}/activities
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "MEETING", "direction": "OUTBOUND", "subject": "Demo call" }

### Quotation sent
POST {{host}}/api/leads/{{leadId}}/activities
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "QUOTATION", "direction": "OUTBOUND", "subject": "Quote #4471 — ₹1,25,000" }

### A note is NOT contact — check `advanced` comes back empty of milestones
POST {{host}}/api/leads/{{leadId}}/activities
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "NOTE", "direction": "INTERNAL", "body": "Procurement signs off on Friday" }

### Forging a system entry — expect 422
POST {{host}}/api/leads/{{leadId}}/activities
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "STAGE_CHANGED" }

### Move it forward
PUT {{host}}/api/leads/{{leadId}}/stage
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stageKey": "quotation", "note": "Quote is with them" }

### Drag it back — milestones must survive, which is the point of the design
PUT {{host}}/api/leads/{{leadId}}/stage
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stageKey": "follow_up" }

### The lead now: `stage` says follow_up, `journey.quotationSentAt` is still set
GET {{host}}/api/leads/{{leadId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}

### The complete timeline
GET {{host}}/api/leads/{{leadId}}/timeline?order=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}

### Only human-logged work
GET {{host}}/api/leads/{{leadId}}/timeline?excludeSystem=true
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}

### Close it won
PUT {{host}}/api/leads/{{leadId}}/stage
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stageKey": "won" }

### Marking a lead lost with no reason — expect 422
PUT {{host}}/api/leads/{{leadId}}/stage
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stageKey": "lost" }

### --- Reporting ---

### The funnel, and where the journey breaks
GET {{host}}/api/leads/funnel
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}

### Split by source
GET {{host}}/api/leads/funnel?groupBy=source
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}

### Split by salesperson
GET {{host}}/api/leads/funnel?groupBy=owner
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}

### --- The queues a manager actually works from ---

### Nobody owns these
GET {{host}}/api/leads?unassigned=true
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}

### Open and untouched for a week
GET {{host}}/api/leads?staleForDays=7&status=OPEN
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}

### By channel
GET {{host}}/api/leads?channel=WHATSAPP,INSTAGRAM
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}

### Biggest deals first
GET {{host}}/api/leads?sort=estimatedValue&order=desc&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}

### An unknown value in a list filter is a 422, not a silent widening
GET {{host}}/api/leads?status=WON,MAYBE
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}

### --- Pipeline configuration ---

### A finer-grained source
POST {{host}}/api/lead-sources
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Google Ads — Brand", "channel": "GOOGLE_ADS", "key": "google_ads_brand" }

### A stage of your own — records no milestone, because only you know what it means
POST {{host}}/api/lead-stages
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Negotiation", "position": 6 }

### Deleting a system stage — expect 409
DELETE {{host}}/api/lead-stages/REPLACE_WITH_WON_STAGE_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{la}}
